@* Two ways, and the first is the one to reach for. A button that starts an Unpoly request grows
   its own spinner from `.up-active` — no parameter, no state, and it clears itself when the
   request ends. <Spinner> is for the other case: a button whose work is not a request. *@
<div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
    <form method="post" action="/orders/3201/refund" up-target=".preview" up-disable>
        <AntiforgeryToken />
        <Button Type="submit">Refund — spins by itself</Button>
    </form>

    <Button disabled><Spinner />Saving…</Button>
    <Button Variant="outline" disabled><Spinner />Please wait</Button>
</div>
